WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:02.849
(audience applauds)
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.849 --> 00:00:03.828
(audience applauds)

00:00:03.828 --> 00:00:05.673
- [Kelly] Hello, It's nice to
see you. Have y'all ever met?

00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:06.669
- No, we haven't met before.
- No, no.

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:08.370
I was thinking, I've gotta ask you

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.450
for some dance moves, man.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.283
- Oh man, I've got you,
I've got you covered.

00:00:10.283 --> 00:00:11.116
- Yeah, you can boogie.
- Yeah.

00:00:11.116 --> 00:00:12.300
- I can tell, he can boogie.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.490
- I was gonna ask you, do you
dance? Do you like dancing?

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.050
- I like dancing, but...
- Yeah.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.638
- I can't say anything about
dancing sitting next to him.

00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:18.570
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.730
- Listen, anybody can
dance, everybody can dance.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.454
- That's right, that's right.
- That's a lie. (Kelly laughs)

00:00:22.454 --> 00:00:23.287
- [Jay] You've just gotta feel it right?

00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:24.957
I've gotta tell you one
thing though, before...

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:25.790
- [Kelly] What?

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.790
- Before we move on.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.917
My mom, told me, she's like,

00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.010
"When you go out there, just,

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.600
just tell her I voted for her".

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.340
I'm like, "Mom, that is old news.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.173
I don't think she wants to hear that".

00:00:36.173 --> 00:00:37.901
- It's not old news, it's
still why I'm sitting here.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:39.002
- But she supported you.
- So, I'm appreciative, yeah.

00:00:39.002 --> 00:00:39.930
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.330
And she really loves you and
she wanted me to tell you that.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.941
And she's gonna be very happy
that I said that on the stage.

00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:46.843
- Oh, that's so, that's so awesome.

00:00:46.843 --> 00:00:48.840
(audience applauds) I'm not,
this isn't like, lip service.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.850
I, people still come up to me in Target

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.980
and say that all the time and
I'm like, really thankful.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:53.860
- [Jay] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.020
- Like, and it's a cool
way to have a career,

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.140
like, people wanted an album from me,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.191
- They wanted you, yeah.
- They voted you in.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.024
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:00.038
- [Kelly] Like that's a
cool way to have a career.

00:01:00.038 --> 00:01:00.871
- It is really cool.

00:01:00.871 --> 00:01:02.654
- [Kelly] Yeah, so I'm thankful,
I love it. (Jay laughs)

00:01:02.654 --> 00:01:03.487
We need, we need to talk

00:01:03.487 --> 00:01:04.530
about the new season of "Magnum P.I."

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.392
So, what can you tell us about
what's happening right now?

00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:10.320
- The new season is a lot of the same.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.420
There's a lot of action, a lot of fun.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.900
There's this, very strong
family sort of quality

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.030
to all the characters in the show.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.863
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:18.863 --> 00:01:20.130
- [Jay] So, so I mean, it's kind of,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.399
all the stuff that we expect,
but I also direct an episode.

00:01:24.399 --> 00:01:25.232
- Oh, is that something
you're interested in doing?

00:01:25.232 --> 00:01:26.143
- I directed one last...
- That's cool.

00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:27.540
- I love it, I love it.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.270
It's, it's this really,
kind of interesting thing

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.370
where as an actor, Jay Hernandez,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.380
the individual has to
kind of stay in his lane.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.743
- [Kelly] Hmm.

00:01:35.743 --> 00:01:36.750
- But as a director, you can kind of,

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.120
go outside and play outside
the boundaries a little bit.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.051
So, that's one thing that I love about it.

00:01:40.051 --> 00:01:40.884
- [Kelly] It's interesting because I,

00:01:40.884 --> 00:01:42.270
I've never had any interest of behind the,

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.000
like I've just never, I,
it's just never pulled at me.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.320
And it's interesting, like,

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.000
I feel like it's actors
a lot of times too.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.130
Like, y'all not, not just musicians,

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.110
it's like actors really
like to be a part of

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.180
the whole story, not just
their one characters.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.090
I find that a lot on the couch.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:55.923
- [Jay] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:55.923 --> 00:01:57.180
I think, I think what it is,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.830
is like, there's just a type of freedom

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.240
that you have as a director

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.730
that you don't necessarily
have as an actor,

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.980
because you know, you're
just not afforded the liberty

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.980
to play a million different
characters sometimes.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:08.813
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:08.813 --> 00:02:09.646
- You know, like whatever they think I am,

00:02:09.646 --> 00:02:11.520
it's like I've gotta kind
of stay in that lane.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.244
- [Kelly] I hate that when
people get type casted.

00:02:13.244 --> 00:02:14.160
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.300
- What's the craziest stunt though?

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.763
because it's, it's action
packed, so like what...

00:02:16.763 --> 00:02:17.772
- [Jay] There's a,
there's a lot of action.

00:02:17.772 --> 00:02:18.902
- Do you like the action, doing all that?

00:02:18.902 --> 00:02:19.735
- I love it, I love it.
- Okay.

00:02:19.735 --> 00:02:21.990
- Yeah, I, I absolutely love it.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.613
I don't love it when I have,

00:02:23.613 --> 00:02:25.830
like a two pound burrito
and then got to sprint

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.150
on top of a rooftop or
something like that.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:27.983
(Kelly chuckles)
- Yeah.

00:02:27.983 --> 00:02:31.200
- Don't love that, but I've
done everything on the show.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.650
Car stunts, like guns,
like chasing people,

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.820
fight scenes, all that stuff.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.280
But one of the coolest things was,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.269
in the episode I directed last season.

00:02:40.269 --> 00:02:41.102
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:41.102 --> 00:02:42.630
- I was, we were doing
this underwater stuff

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.760
and it was just like this easy shot

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.680
of me kind of like,
floating through the ocean

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.750
looking for some sunken vessel and...

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:50.583
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:52.458
- And, and, well that's not
the coolest part about it.

00:02:52.458 --> 00:02:53.291
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:55.500
- So I'm, I'm like, probably
60 feet under the surface

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.500
of the ocean and the
coordinator, stunt guy,

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.923
he tells me to turn around and I,

00:02:59.923 --> 00:03:02.610
I turn around and there was a pod of like,

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.470
60 dolphins that were...
- Amazing.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.610
- Swimming by.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:08.132
And you see like the little,
like the little baby ones.

00:03:08.132 --> 00:03:08.965
- [Derek] The baby ones are best.

00:03:08.965 --> 00:03:10.260
- [Jay] They were playing
around with the, with the...

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.093
- Yeah.
- With the older ones.

00:03:11.093 --> 00:03:11.926
- [Kelly] That's magical.

00:03:11.926 --> 00:03:14.880
- It was like, surreal,
magical, it was crazy.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.550
And it was, it felt
like I really understood

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.020
that they were a family.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.450
It was the strangest experience,

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.340
but it was just beautiful.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.500
- I mean, you, we don't pause enough.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.180
Like, that's a moment that like,

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.340
not really anyone's gonna have.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.173
- Yeah, no, and and...

00:03:30.173 --> 00:03:31.006
- Do you know what I'm
saying? How special was that?

00:03:31.006 --> 00:03:32.070
- It was work for me, you know?

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.189
Like I was, I was
getting paid to be there.

00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:34.022
- Yeah.

00:03:34.022 --> 00:03:35.200
- Like, I would pay for
that experience, but.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.330
- Yeah.
- Yeah, it's...

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.370
- But nobody gets that kind of experience

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.203
just out in the wild.

00:03:39.203 --> 00:03:40.500
That's like really cool.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.333
- [Jay] Yeah, it was beautiful.

00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:42.390
- I can't imagine the energy off of that.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.010
What's like the wildest or most like,

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.638
dangerous thing you've done on stage or?

00:03:45.638 --> 00:03:46.558
- Well...
- Or in life?

00:03:46.558 --> 00:03:47.850
- Well, I, I'm, I'm kind of similar.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.040
I, I love skydiving, I love crazy stuff.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.080
And swimming with dolphins
or humpback whales

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.940
in Tonga has been incredible.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.140
But, there was this one experience...

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.110
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:56.943
- [Derek] You, you know Bear Grylls?

00:03:56.943 --> 00:03:57.776
- Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:57.776 --> 00:03:58.980
- So, I went on an adventure with him

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.080
and we were in Bulgaria
and we went skydive,

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.850
after we were in this,
swimming in a glacier lake.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.110
We get in this helicopter, we go up,

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.263
and he's like,

00:04:05.263 --> 00:04:06.540
"Derek, All right, this
is what we're gonna do,

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.190
we're gonna just jump outta
this helicopter, da da da".

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.410
And there's this guy with
this like, black mask on

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.607
and I get in there,
strap in, and we're like,

00:04:12.607 --> 00:04:14.470
"Oh, we've gotta jump out now, now, now".

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.870
And I'm realizing that I don't
have these straps here in.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:18.757
- Oh, no.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:21.487
- And then, I'm hanging out
the window and I'm like,

00:04:21.487 --> 00:04:23.937
"I'm not strapped in!
I'm not strapped in!"

00:04:23.937 --> 00:04:26.250
And he's like, "One, two..."

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.083
- Oh, my god.

00:04:27.083 --> 00:04:28.050
- "Okay, now let's do it for real.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.340
Let's get you strapped in".

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:30.173
(audience laughs)

00:04:30.173 --> 00:04:33.505
And I was like, I, I, I
thought it was the end of me.

00:04:33.505 --> 00:04:36.405
(Kelly gasps)
(audience applauds)

00:04:36.405 --> 00:04:37.238
- [Kelly] Like, I...

00:04:37.238 --> 00:04:38.460
- I thought, I thought,
I was like, "This is it.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.810
I'm gonna die, here we go".

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.280
- I was not breathing in that story

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.315
and I didn't realize it until the release.

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:44.160
- [Derek] Yeah.
(Derek chuckles)

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.700
- Like, wow, what a way
to mess with someone.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.533
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:50.148
- He did that on purpose
making, like obviously, like.

00:04:50.148 --> 00:04:52.740
- I feel like he's done
that more than once.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.017
Like, he likes screwing with people.

00:04:54.017 --> 00:04:54.850
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.160
- I, there might have
been a little bit of,

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.676
something coming out, you know.

00:04:57.676 --> 00:04:58.509
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:58.509 --> 00:04:59.342
- [Kelly] Yeah, right.

00:04:59.342 --> 00:05:01.263
The glacier water changed color.

